WEBVTT

00:02.410 --> 00:07.920
<u>I  LOVE  ANIME</u>

00:02.410 --> 00:07.920
STUDIO  RIVA - Nyo

00:02.410 --> 00:07.920
<b>#ILA @ Rizon</b>

00:06.220 --> 00:12.920
<b>Sekai de ichiban kagayakeru made</b>

00:13.490 --> 00:19.260
<b>Ichinichi mainichi wo tanoshiku ikite</b>

00:19.500 --> 00:24.770
<b>Totsuzen umarekuru setsuna no fuan</b>

00:25.270 --> 00:31.370
<b>2000-nen mondai yori
jibun no yume</b>

00:31.480 --> 00:37.350
<b>Sekai de ichiban kagayakitai</b>

00:37.450 --> 00:40.420
<b>Omoi wa number 1 star</b>

00:40.520 --> 00:43.490
<b>Kono sora no naka de</b>

00:51.330 --> 00:54.260
<b>Hello, everyone.
I hear there is someone here...</b>

00:54.370 --> 00:57.030
<b>who adds a weird word
to the end of their sentences.</b>

00:57.870 --> 00:59.930
<b>I need to talk to them about that.</b>

01:00.210 --> 01:01.170
<b>Gamers Open</b>

01:02.110 --> 01:03.170
<b>This one, please.</b>

01:03.280 --> 01:04.900
<b>Welcome to our store nyo.</b>

01:05.410 --> 01:07.470
<b>I'd like to buy it
with my point card please.</b>

01:07.580 --> 01:09.480
<b>You have many points nyo.</b>

01:10.450 --> 01:13.680
<b>Please fill out this information
with your name and address nyo.</b>

01:13.790 --> 01:15.410
<b>Of course.</b>

01:15.520 --> 01:17.150
<b>Here you go.</b>

01:17.590 --> 01:19.490
<b>Thank you very much nyo.</b>

01:20.060 --> 01:21.550
<b>No, thank you!</b>

01:21.660 --> 01:23.630
<b>Gema
I am muchi muchi.</b>

01:23.730 --> 01:25.200
<b>Do you like muchi muchi?</b>

01:25.300 --> 01:27.420
<b>Dejiko-chan, I'm rooting for you.</b>

01:27.530 --> 01:28.790
<b>I'll try my best nyo.</b>

01:28.900 --> 01:30.960
<b>I am full of meat.
Do you like meat!?</b>

01:32.940 --> 01:36.030
<b>It looks like that customer
is head over heels for me nyo.</b>

01:36.140 --> 01:36.870
<b>It's you!</b>

01:36.980 --> 01:37.370
<b>Nyo?</b>

01:37.480 --> 01:40.040
<b>Words are a beautiful thing.</b>

01:40.150 --> 01:44.780
<b>Words are passed down from our ancestors
as proof that humans existed.</b>

01:44.880 --> 01:48.840
<b>That's why words must be elegant.
But...</b>

01:50.960 --> 01:52.790
<b>What the heck is ''nyo?''</b>

01:52.890 --> 01:53.520
<b>Nyo...</b>

01:53.630 --> 01:56.190
<b>Do you always put ''nyo''
at the end of your sentences?</b>

01:56.290 --> 01:57.630
<b>Who did you learn that from?</b>

01:57.730 --> 01:59.220
<b>It's original nyo.</b>

01:59.330 --> 02:00.960
<b>I see, original.</b>

02:01.070 --> 02:01.860
<b>Gunyo.</b>

02:01.970 --> 02:04.990
<b>This is not good.</b>

02:05.100 --> 02:08.100
<b>Don't you agree?
See here.</b>

02:08.870 --> 02:15.140
<b>Kanji : Rou Nyaku Nan Nyo</b>

02:08.870 --> 02:13.440
<b>It means ''all those who are
young, old, men, or women.''</b>

02:13.550 --> 02:15.140
<b>Rounyakunannyo.</b>

02:15.250 --> 02:18.150
<b>You would probably say
''Rounyakunannyo nyo.''</b>

02:18.250 --> 02:21.520
<b>There's more. In Italy,
there's a region called Bologna.</b>

02:21.620 --> 02:23.650
<b>You'd probably say ''Bologna nyo.''</b>

02:23.760 --> 02:26.050
<b>The Buddhist word Nyorai...
Let me get this.</b>

02:26.160 --> 02:28.590
<b>you'd say '' Nyorai nyo.''
Welcome nyo.</b>

02:29.090 --> 02:31.060
<b>Thank you very much nyo.
I'll come again nyo.</b>

02:31.160 --> 02:32.760
<b>Will you stop saying that ''nyo?''</b>

02:32.860 --> 02:34.920
<b>No way nyo.
I won't stop nyo. Try me nyo.</b>

02:35.930 --> 02:38.840
<b>The language is crumbling.</b>

02:38.940 --> 02:40.170
<b>I hit something gema.</b>

02:40.810 --> 02:42.540
<b>Now it's ''gema!''</b>

02:42.640 --> 02:45.170
<b>What do you put on sweet rice?
''Goma shio gema.''</b>

02:45.280 --> 02:48.250
<b>What do you call that thing on a
sumo wrestler's head? ''Mage gema.''</b>

02:48.350 --> 02:50.810
<b>Inside a volcano?
''Magma gema...''</b>

02:52.050 --> 02:54.990
<b>I want that nyo.
I want this gema.</b>

02:55.090 --> 02:56.550
<b>I'm tired gema.</b>

02:56.660 --> 02:58.780
<b>It's come down to this...</b>

03:02.490 --> 03:03.190
<b>Nyu.</b>

03:07.170 --> 03:08.190
<b>H-hi.</b>

03:08.300 --> 03:12.460
<b>What a cute girl.
She brings me happiness.</b>

03:13.100 --> 03:17.200
<b>Nice to meet you.
My name is Takuro Kimura.</b>

03:17.310 --> 03:18.800
<b>What's your name?</b>

03:18.910 --> 03:20.040
<b>Petit Charat nyu.</b>

03:20.150 --> 03:23.480
<b>Oh. Petit Charat-chan. I see.</b>

03:23.580 --> 03:24.610
<b>Nyu?</b>

03:24.720 --> 03:27.550
<b>Did she just say ''nyu''?
Yeah, I think she did.</b>

03:27.650 --> 03:29.280
<b>That means she says
''Gyuunyuu nyu...''</b>

03:29.390 --> 03:31.080
<b>and ''Champagne nyu...''
Nyu!</b>

03:31.790 --> 03:33.920
<b>Do I really have to tell
this cute girl...</b>

03:34.030 --> 03:37.090
<b>not to add weird words
to the end of her sentences?</b>

03:37.200 --> 03:39.490
<b>What should I do?
What should I do?</b>

03:40.200 --> 03:41.720
<b>I'll take this please.</b>

03:41.830 --> 03:45.000
<b>Puchiko is not for sale nyo!</b>

03:41.830 --> 03:45.000
<b>Takuro Kimura (Murataku)
Pseudo student, lives in a mansion</b>
